:HELP NAME=FNDSTRPDM.Find String Using PDM (FNDSTRPDM)
:P.Use the Find String Using PDM (FNDSTRPDM) command to find a string in
a file's members, then run an option on each member that has it or print
what was found.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/STRING'.Find string (STRING)
:P.The find string for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 40 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/OPTION'.Operation (OPTION)
:P.The operation for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Prompt
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/PRTMBRLIST'.Print list (PRTMBRLIST)
:P.Whether to print list.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/PRTRCDS'.Print records (PRTRCDS)
:P.The print records for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/COL'.Columns to search (COL)
:P.The columns to search for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. From column
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 228.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. To column
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RCDLEN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/CASE'.Kind of match (CASE)
:P.The kind of match for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IGNORE, *MATCH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FNDSTRPDM/PARM'.Parameters (PARM)
:P.The parameters passed to the program, in order.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 220 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRPDM.Start PDM (STRPDM)
:P.The Start PDM (STRPDM) command works with the Programming Development
Manager's menu.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLIBPDM.Work with Libraries Using PDM (WRKLIBPDM)
:P.The Work with Libraries Using PDM (WRKLIBPDM) command works with the
libraries with PDM's options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIBPDM/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMBRPDM.Work with Members Using PDM (WRKMBRPDM)
:P.The Work with Members Using PDM (WRKMBRPDM) command works with a
file's members with PDM's options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMBRPDM/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMBRPDM/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMBRPDM/MBRTYPE'.Member type (MBRTYPE)
:P.The member type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJPDM.Work with Objects Using PDM (WRKOBJPDM)
:P.The Work with Objects Using PDM (WRKOBJPDM) command works with a
library's objects with PDM's options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJPDM/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJPDM/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJPDM/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
